# OpenCut

A **free, open-source video editor for web, desktop, and mobile**, pulled in
as-is from upstream [`opencut-app/opencut`](https://github.com/opencut-app/opencut)
(the ground-up rewrite — the old version lives at `opencut-app/opencut-classic`
and still runs on opencut.app). This repo is a personal working copy: the code
was not reinvented or restructured, only wrapped in the standard AI Control
scaffold so it can be run, tracked, and iterated on here.

Monorepo (moon + bun workspaces):
- `apps/web` — the editor itself. TanStack Start (React 19) on Vite, deployed
  to Cloudflare via the Cloudflare Vite plugin. `localhost:5173`.
- `apps/api` — a Cloudflare Workers API stub (Elysia). `localhost:8787`.
- `apps/desktop` — Tauri (Rust) desktop shell. See `apps/desktop/README.md`.
- `crates/media` — shared Rust media core.

Per upstream's own README: **the rewrite is early and not yet open to outside
contributions** — an Editor API, plugin architecture, one Rust core across
web/desktop/mobile, an MCP server, headless/automation mode, and an in-editor
scripting tab are all still landing. Treat this as tracking a moving target,
not a finished app.

## How to run
```sh
cd apps/web && bun install && bun run dev   # http://localhost:5173
```
Verified working 2026-11-06: `bun install` (576 packages) then `bun run dev`
serves the real OpenCut page via Vite + the Cloudflare adapter, no errors.
The API (`cd apps/api && bun install && bun run dev`) and desktop app were not
exercised yet — desktop needs the Rust/Tauri toolchain (`.prototools` pins
`rust = 1.97.0`, machine has 1.97.1) and is unverified.

Upstream also expects `proto` + `moon` for the full pinned-toolchain, cross-app
`moon run <app>:dev` workflow; neither is installed here yet — `bun` alone is
enough to run `apps/web`. See `.prototools` for pinned versions.

## Secrets
None needed to run the app locally. `.env.example` (`R2_BUCKET=opencut-assets`)
is only for the ops-only `upload-logos` moon task (pushes brand SVGs to
Cloudflare R2) — not required for dev or build.

## Status
Pulled in under AI Control on 2026-11-06, upstream git history dropped (this
repo starts its own history). `apps/web` installs and runs clean. See
`issues.txt` for what's unverified and `updates/2026-11-06 INIT - OPEN/` for
the setup record.
